WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(chopping sounds)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:03.610
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.260
- [Zoe] The American South has long had

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:07.010
a taste for Mexican food.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.270
But one chef has created a unique fusion

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.103
of his very own.

00:00:30.736 --> 00:00:33.210
- I'm Zoe Saldana from BESE,

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.100
and I'm teaming up with Great Big Story

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.010
to shine a light on
American LatinX Excellence

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:38.963
around the country.

00:00:42.784 --> 00:00:45.520
(fast upbeat music)

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.353
(clicking noises)

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:56.740
- [Zoe] Eddie came to the
U.S. as a teenager in 1974,

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:59.313
with just $140 in his pocket.

00:01:06.376 --> 00:01:07.540
(running water)

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.840
- [Zoe] Today, he runs
a string of restaurants

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.090
in Georgia and Tennessee.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:14.300
His success is undeniably due to his

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.003
clever approach to each dish.

00:01:24.466 --> 00:01:27.049
(upbeat music)

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.880
- [Zoe] While Eddie utilizes
ingredients native to Mexico,

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.003
he keeps the American pallet in mind.

00:02:04.258 --> 00:02:06.336
(upbeat music)

00:02:06.336 --> 00:02:10.390
- [Zoe] For Eddie, each dish
takes time and experimentation.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.503
But the end result is always worth it.

00:02:26.059 --> 00:02:28.381
(dish scraping)

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.964
(upbeat music)

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:52.166
(chopping sounds)

00:02:56.715 --> 00:02:59.798
(high pinging noise)

